  "contracts": [
    "One N05 mutable map owner, N10 flags/counters, N11 glyph-shared phase/state and previous FC reference; no duplicate authoritative world.",
    "Native event cadence and measured preceding-service C2; signed LOWWORD/min8 door extent, signed DWORD conveyor divisor. No fixed30 substitute.",
    "Separate ordered public action/motion controls latches retain short pulses; Use release outside dispatch and pause UI clears both.",
    "Native OPEN/CLOSE/AUTO queue/occupancy/keys and sensor glyph identity preserved, owner registration occurs before dispatch.",
    "Direct conveyor wrapper invokes native resolver and occupancy once, including legal displacement350 at C2=4; ordinary N09 quarter guard remains separate.",
    "Render uses copied phase view, preserves phase0 N07 packets and source UV mirror/crop, never mutates simulation/camera history."
  ],
  "explicit_adaptations": [
    "Fully-open panels are suppressed at extent>1 and phase>=extent-1 to eliminate native residual strips. Constructor phase0/extent1 stays visible.",
    "Repeated ready-open Use may resample a smaller extent while phase stays larger; this legal source domain is hidden until subsequent CLOSE reaches a cropped phase. Public API regression and shared ARM9 renderer tests cover it.",
    "Six controlled floor poses inside closed door L2 K are NDS bounded guards; not claimed native equivalence or admitted gameplay starts.",
    "FINISH output substitutes native health=-1 without campaign transition or latch; other STAT/audio/UI consumers remain later tasks.",
    "Keys/score/repositioning/controlled occupancy are explicit diagnostic fixtures; A advances probe stages, not gameplay."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Physical DS/DS Lite, flashcart/loader, actual FPS/latency/IRQ/stack peak deferred to final N24.",
    "Isolated original x86 instructions with intercepted services, not a complete DOS/DPMI game session.",
    "N11 live route has zero ordinary motion substeps; N09/N10 supply navigation evidence. Seven actual conveyor callbacks replayed.",
    "Linux x86_64-musl compiled/linked only, not executed in Windows.",
    "0/30/60 comparisons use the same explicit input/service timeline; different polling schedules are not equated.",
    "Vertical middle frames show upward texture/crossbar motion; visible intermediate gap is established by horizontal pairs, terminal clearance by all four open frames.",
